          <h2 class="heading-border heading-center heading-left mb-4 pb-3 d-inline-block">The Challenge</h2>
          <p class="large-para mb-3">
            Process serving companies are legally required to provide sworn affidavits of service to courts and law firms. These documents must meet strict formatting requirements, include specific evidence (GPS, timestamp, server identity, method of service), and be signed by both the process server and a commissioner of oaths.
          </p>
          <p class="large-para mb-0">
            Generating these documents manually took 30-45 minutes per case: pulling field notes from email threads, formatting them into a Word template, exporting to PDF, emailing for signatures, tracking signature status, and emailing the final document to the firm. Errors in affidavit format caused rejection by courts, requiring the entire process to restart.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="col-12 col-lg-5">
          <div class="workflow-card p-4">
            <h3 class="h6 text-uppercase text-muted mb-3">Quick Stats</h3>
            <ul class="mb-0 ps-3 small" style="line-height: 1.8;">
              <li><strong>Tech:</strong> WeasyPrint, DocuSign API, Gemini Pro (narrative generation), PostgreSQL (case data source), Mailgun (delivery), AWS S3 (document storage)</li>
              <li><strong>Result:</strong> Affidavit generation time reduced from 45 minutes to under 2 minutes. Zero formatting rejections. Complete signing audit trail captured in DocuSign. Law firms receive signed documents within minutes of service confirmation.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-5 bg-light-grey">
