        <h2 class="heading-border heading-center mb-4 pb-3 d-inline-block">The Solution</h2>
        <p class="large-para mb-3">
          An automated affidavit pipeline integrated directly into the case lifecycle. When service is confirmed, the system generates a legally-formatted sworn affidavit from a WeasyPrint HTML/CSS template, pre-populated entirely from structured case data: server identity, license number, case details, service target, date/time/GPS of each attempt, method of service, and the specific documents served. No manual entry. No copy-paste.
        </p>
        <p class="large-para mb-0">
          The document routes through DocuSign in the legally required signing order: process server signs first, then commissioner of oaths signs. Once both signatures are captured, the signed PDF is automatically emailed to the law firm. When service fails, the AI generates a formal non-service narrative for court submission, structured legal language derived from the server's informal field notes.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
